  "id": "DrugBank_DB00860 - MONDO_4979",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Asthma through a series of interconnected pathways, primarily involving corticosteroid receptor activation and immune modulation. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone may act as a therapeutic agent for Asthma through its ability to modulate inflammatory responses, as indicated by its association with Erythema Multiforme and Inherited Isolated Adrenal Insufficiency Due To Partial Cyp11a1 Deficiency. These conditions, in turn, are linked to Asthma, indicating a potential role for Prednisolone in the management of inflammatory diseases. The presence of Methylprednisolone as a downstream target in these pathways further supports the notion that Prednisolone may exert a beneficial effect on Asthma by suppressing inflammation and immune overactivation. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of corticosteroid action in the treatment of Asthma, with Prednisolone potentially serving as a key therapeutic agent through its well-documented anti-inflammatory effects.",
